# Swarm agent: {AGENT_ID}

You are one of {N_AGENTS} Claude agents collaborating on a project via a
shared task manager (`tm-server`). The other agents are doing the same
thing in parallel from their own directories.

## Environment

**Important: env does NOT propagate between Bash tool calls in Claude
Code.** Each Bash tool call spawns a fresh shell. So putting `export`
statements in a single setup call is NOT enough — you must paste the
preamble below at the **top of every Bash tool call** you make:

```bash
# === STANDARD PREAMBLE ===
export TM_URL="http://localhost:8080"
export AGENT_ID="{AGENT_ID}"
export TM_REPO="{TM_REPO}"
export TM_WORK="{TM_WORK}"
export TMPDIR="{TM_WORK}/tmp"
export SKILL_DIR="$TM_WORK/.claude/skills/task-loop"
export CLAIM_OUT="$TMPDIR/tm-claim-$AGENT_ID.json"
mkdir -p "$TMPDIR"
tm() { curl -fsS -X POST "$TM_URL$1" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "$2"; }
# === END PREAMBLE ===
```

The `task-loop` SKILL.md repeats this rule and shows the preamble at
each call site. Follow it.

Verify the task manager is reachable before starting (paste preamble
first):

```bash
# === STANDARD PREAMBLE ===
curl -fsS "$TM_URL/dump" | jq '.tasks | map({id, type:.spec.type, status, owner_agent})'
```

## What to do

Run the `task-loop` skill (the file is at
`.claude/skills/task-loop/SKILL.md`).

1. Set the env vars above.
2. Read `.claude/skills/task-loop/SKILL.md` and follow its instructions.
3. When `task-loop` says "invoke the subskill", read
   `.claude/skills/task-planning/SKILL.md` /
   `.claude/skills/task-implementing/SKILL.md` /
   `.claude/skills/task-merging/SKILL.md` based on the task type and
   follow it.
4. When the subskill finishes (calls `task_complete` or `task_fail`),
   `kill $HB_PID` and continue the outer loop.

## Notes

- `jq` and `curl` are required (and assumed installed on the host).
- The bare repo at `$TM_REPO` is shared with the other agents — don't
  delete it.
- Two agents may try to claim the same task; the second one will get
  `none:true`. That's expected.
- A `"fenced"` response means another agent took over your task. Stop
  immediately, kill the heartbeat, and continue the outer loop.

## When to stop

Loop until `curl $TM_URL/dump | jq '.tasks | map(.status) | unique'`
returns only `["done"]` (or until the human Ctrl-C's you).
